=========================================================================
🚀 MODULE 4: LIST & MULTIMEDIA CONTROL (ADVANCED ATTRIBUTES)
=========================================================================
Description: Web pages par data ko organized structural format mein dikhana 
aur modern browsers ke mutabik Audio/Video media engines ko control karna.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. LIST TYPES (Data Ko Organize Karne Ka Tareeka)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HTML mein content ko list format mein dikhane ke liye main do tarike hote hain:

* Unordered List (<ul>):
  Yeh bullet points banane ke liye use hota hai. Iska default visual style 
  ek solid dot (disc) hota hai, jise hum CSS ke zariye badal sakte hain.

* Ordered List (<ol>):
  Yeh data ki proper numbering (1, 2, 3...) karne ke liye use hota hai. 
  HTML5 ke andar iske paas kuch bohot useful aur cool attributes hain:
  1. type="..." ──> Isse aap numbering ka format badal sakte ho.
     - type="A" (Capital letters: A, B, C...)
     - type="a" (Small letters: a, b, c...)
     - type="I" (Capital Roman numbers: I, II, III...)
     - type="i" (Small Roman numbers: i, ii, iii...)
  2. start="..." ──> Isse aap numbering ki starting position control kar sakte ho.
     Agar start="5" likha hai, toh ginti seedhe 5 se shuru hogi.

🛠️ LIVE CODE EXAMPLE FOR LISTS:
<ol type="I" start="3">
    <li>HTML Core</li>    <!-- Output: III. HTML Core -->
    <li>CSS Styling</li>   <!-- Output: IV. CSS Styling -->
</ol>

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MULTIMEDIA DEEP CONTROL (<video> & <audio>)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HTML5 mein multimedia ko setup karne ke liye external software nahi lagte, 
lekin user experience ko top-notch banane ke liye high-level attributes hote hain:

🛠️ ADVANCED MULTIMEDIA ATTRIBUTES:
* controls: Video/Audio ke niche play, pause, aur volume ke native buttons dikhata hai.
* autoplay: Web page load hote hi media file apne aap chalne lagti hai.
* muted: Media bina kisi aawaz (silent mode) ke shuru hota hai.
  ⚠️ BROWSER SECURITY RULE: Aaj kal ke modern browsers (Chrome, Safari, Edge) 
  bina 'muted' attribute ke 'autoplay' ko block kar dete hain, taaki website 
  open hote hi sudden tez aawaz se user pareshan na ho.
* loop: Video/Audio khatam hote hi apne aap dobara zero se shuru ho jayegi 
  (Jaise Instagram Reels ya YouTube Loops).
* poster="...": Video chalne se pehle screen par jo Thumbnail photo dikhata hai, 
  wo isi attribute ke raste lagayi jaati hai.

🛠️ LIVE CODE EXAMPLE FOR MULTIMEDIA:
<video controls autoplay muted loop poster="thumbnail.jpg" width="600">
    <source src="course-video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    <!-- Browser fallback text agar format support na kare -->
    Aapka browser video tag support nahi karta hai.
</video>

=========================================================================
=== END OF MODULE 4 NOTES ===
